  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;MARION JESSIE THOMPSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marion Jessie Thompson is a woman of mystery born in 1890, whose life has been largely shrouded in secrecy, but recent discoveries have revealed her marriage to Dows Dunham and Ruby Frewen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marion Jessie Thompson is part of an enigmatic couple whose marriage has sparked public interest and debate."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOWS DUNHAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dows Dunham is a renowned American archaeologist who was married to Marion Jessie Thompson from 1922 until his death, and was also married to Ruby Frewen, who died in 1866."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUBY FREWEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ruby Frewen is a person who died in 1866, but Marion Jessie Thompson claims to be married to him, creating a mysterious and seemingly impossible union."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ruby Frewen is part of an enigmatic couple whose marriage has sparked public interest and debate."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW YORK STATE ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New York State Archives provided marriage records confirming the union between Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALBANY, NEW YORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Albany, New York is the location where Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham got married on June 24, 1922."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. PETER LACOVARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Peter Lacovara is a leading expert on ancient Egyptian archaeology who corroborated the findings about Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham's marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSEUM RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Museum Records at the Metropolitan Museum of Art show that Marion Jessie Thompson frequently visited the museum, often accompanying her husband to exhibitions and events."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARVARD UNIVERSITY ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harvard University Archives house a series of letters exchanged between Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham, revealing a deep affection and mutual respect between the couple."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. KATHRYN BARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Kathryn Bard is a professor of archaeology at Boston University who commented on the significance of the marriage between Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. EMILY WILSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Emily Wilson is a renowned historian specializing in 19th-century British history who expressed disbelief at the revelation of Marion Jessie Thompson's marriage to Ruby Frewen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. JAMES REED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. James Reed is a leading expert in historical correspondence who analyzed the letters and diaries suggesting a deep emotional connection between Marion Jessie Thompson and Ruby Frewen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METROPOLITAN MUSEUM OF ART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Metropolitan Museum of Art is a location where Dows Dunham served as the curator of the Egyptian Department from 1935 to 1960, and where Marion Jessie Thompson was a frequent visitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOSTON UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boston University is a location where Dr. Kathryn Bard teaches archaeology and commented on the significance of the marriage between Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARVARD UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harvard University is a location where the letters and diaries between Marion Jessie Thompson and Dows Dunham are housed."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEWSPAPER ARTICLE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A newspaper article published breaking news about Marion Jessie Thompson's marriage to Dows Dunham, providing evidence and insights into their relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEWSPAPER ARTICLE 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A newspaper article published breaking news about Marion Jessie Thompson's marriage to Ruby Frewen, creating a mystery and sparking debate in the academic community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOWS DUNHAM'S MARRIAGE RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marriage records confirm the union between Dows Dunham and Marion Jessie Thompson."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LETTERS AND DIARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
